---
/**
 * CaseStudies.astro — Proof, Not Promises. Used on / and /services/.
 * Rebuilt Sep 2026 as before/after panels, one literal scene per story (shop →
 * three sales channels; a 5-day week → a phone chat; cash leaving → cash kept), the real results in big type, and the
 * full story behind "Read the full story". All figures and copy below were
 * already live in the July–August 2026 version; do not add new ones.
 *
 * Client case study — anonymised: figures yes, names never. The build gate
 * (scripts/audit-build.mjs) fails on a client name, including in comments,
 * because Astro renders JSX comments into the HTML.
 *
 * Own-build card ("Built without waiting"). Replaced an auto-shop client case
 * study on 2026-08-02: that project was a first trial done for family, it is
 * being handed over, and there was nothing shippable to point at. The client
 * card answers "has he done this for someone like me", this one answers "can
 * he actually build at this level". Keep both. Cutting either leaves an
 * obvious hole.
 *
 * FRAMING — do not undo this. The own-build card is about SPEED, not
 * headcount. Greg's point (2026-08-02) is that every change used to require
 * going to a developer and waiting days; now he makes it himself, often from
 * his phone, and it is live immediately. That is the thing clients actually
 * buy, and it is a pain every business owner has felt. Never write "I fired my
 * developers" or any variant. Same underlying fact, but an owner reads it as
 * "this man replaces people" — and it contradicts the position taken at the
 * Oakville meetup, where the honest answer is that AI replaced the agency, not
 * the staff. Client work stays visible on purpose: Greg was explicit that
 * client builds should not be discarded in favour of own-brand work; saying
 * "built for a client" is fine.
 *
 * Own brands — GearTOP + TapeGeeks, safe to name.
 */

const cases = [
  {
    tag: 'Client project',
    scene: 'shop', beforeHead: 'One shop, one door', afterHead: 'Selling online, to companies, at better prices',
    title: 'Traditional retail shop to full e-commerce operation',
    before: 'New owner, 84+ hours a week, zero e-commerce experience',
    after: 'A complete digital operation, delivered in 6 weeks',
    metrics: [['6 weeks', 'delivery time'], ['Six figures', 'added from pricing alone'], ['New channel', 'corporate gifting, built from zero'], ['~2×', 'revenue trajectory']],
    story: ['New owner, one week into a long-established specialty retail business. Zero e-commerce experience. Working 84+ hours a week. Needed a complete digital transformation plan — fast.'],
    listTitle: 'What I built',
    list: [
      '18 deliverable areas — competitive analysis, pricing strategy, SEO, email, social, UGC, partnerships, financial tracking',
      'Custom Content Creator PRO v5.3 — web app for generating platform-specific AI prompts, handed over running',
      'Corporate gifting program with B2B sales materials — a six-figure channel that didn’t exist before',
      'Pricing optimization strategy — a six-figure annual gain from margin adjustments alone',
      'Interactive client dashboard deployed on GitHub Pages — live, browser-based, no downloads',
    ],
    links: [],
  },
  {
    tag: 'Built without waiting',
    scene: 'speed', beforeHead: 'One small change took all week', afterHead: 'Now it takes minutes, from a phone',
    title: 'It used to take days. Now I do it from my phone.',
    before: 'Every change: brief a developer, wait days, review, wait again',
    after: 'Minutes: live before the conversation is over',
    metrics: [['Minutes', 'to ship a change, not days'], ['2', 'apps live in the App Store'], ['12', 'projects shipped'], ['$75K+', 'annual agency cost removed']],
    story: [
      'Every change used to mean going to a developer. A blog post, a price update, a page that needed fixing — write the brief, wait, review it, wait again. Days, every time, for work that took minutes to describe. And nothing shipped while you waited.',
      'That’s the part that changed. I make the change myself now, often from my phone, and it’s live before the conversation is over. Not because I became a programmer — I’m a mechanical engineer and I’ve never written software professionally. Because describing the work precisely is now enough to get it built.',
      'This is the same capability I hand over. When a client wants a page changed, a post published, or a price updated, the answer stops being “I’ll ask the developer and get back to you next week.”',
    ],
    listTitle: 'What’s been shipped that way',
    list: [
      'Two iOS apps, live in the App Store — SunUp, which calculates real burn time from skin type and live UV, and RunMate Pro, GPS tracking with shoe-mileage management. RunMate was rejected 39 times before it was approved.',
      'Helm — seller intelligence that pulls Amazon SP-API, Amazon Ads, Shopify, Meta, Klaviyo and Search Console into one place, then exposes it to Claude as tools.',
      'A full event platform for a chip-timed road race I direct — 875 runners in its first year, plus their families, spectators and 80 local partners.',
      'Two Shopify stores running on API connections, with product content and blog production automated end to end.',
      'SportsClinicFinder — a Canada-wide clinic directory covering every province and territory, searchable by city, injury, and specialty.',
      'Magpie — a shared research brain for the team, so nobody researches the same thing twice.',
      'Marketing sites for both apps, plus this one — statically built, deployed on Vercel, with a post-build audit that fails the deploy on a dead link or a broken image.',
      'Content Creator PRO — built for a client, handed over running, so they stopped needing an agency on retainer to do it.',
    ],
    links: [{ href: '/projects/', label: 'See all of it, with the stack behind each one' }, { href: '/race-directors/', label: 'I build this for other race directors' }],
  },
  {
    tag: 'My businesses',
    scene: 'agency', beforeHead: 'Money out the door every month', afterHead: 'The money stays; the content multiplies',
    title: 'Two e-commerce brands running on AI tools I built myself',
    before: '$75K–$125K a year to agencies, freelancers and services',
    after: 'Systems I built, running every day',
    metrics: [['$75K+', 'annual savings'], ['5–10×', 'content volume'], ['15–20×', 'email marketing ROI'], ['2', 'apps live in the App Store']],
    story: ['Two e-commerce brands. $2M+ in ad spend. Paying $75K-$125K annually for agencies, freelancers, and services. Needed to cut costs without cutting results.'],
    listTitle: 'What I built',
    list: [
      'Custom AI content generation systems (100+ product descriptions, brand voice maintained)',
      'Marketing automation workflows replacing manual email, social, and ad management',
      '2 iOS apps (SunUp by GearTOP, RunMate Pro) — built as a non-coder using AI tools',
      'Analytics dashboards aggregating data from Shopify, Amazon, Google, Meta',
      'Operational automation (inventory alerts, reorder triggers, journey orchestration)',
    ],
    links: [],
  },
];
---

<section id="results" class="cs" aria-labelledby="cs-heading">
  <div class="cs-head">
    <div class="cs-eyebrow">Proof, not promises</div>
    <h2 id="cs-heading">Before and after.</h2>
    <p>Three real jobs. On the left, how it was. On the right, what changed.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cs-list">
    {cases.map((c, i) => (
      <article class="cs-card">
        <div class="cs-top">
          <span class="cs-tag">{c.tag}</span>
          <h3>{c.title}</h3>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-ba">
          {/* BEFORE / AFTER: each story draws its own scene (c.scene) */}
          <figure class="cs-panel cs-before">
            <figcaption class="cs-cap"><span class="cs-pill">Before</span><b>{c.beforeHead}</b></figcaption>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 320 170" aria-hidden="true" data-anim>
              {c.scene === 'shop' && (
                <g>
                  <path d="M6 146 H314" class="floor" />
                  {/* the shop: one door, open 9 to 5 */}
                  <rect x="170" y="62" width="120" height="84" class="bld" />
                  <path d="M162 62 h136 l-8 -20 h-120 z" class="awn" />
                  {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((k) => <path d={`M${170 + k * 20} 42 h10 v20 h-10 z`} class="awn-s" />)}
                  <rect x="214" y="98" width="30" height="48" class="door" />
                  <rect x="180" y="74" width="26" height="20" class="win" /><rect x="254" y="74" width="26" height="20" class="win" />
                  <text x="230" y="36" text-anchor="middle" class="say sm">Owner: 84+ hrs a week</text>
                  {[0, 1].map((k) => (
                    <use href="#i-person" width="28" height="28" class="walker">
                      <animateMotion dur="6s" begin={`-${k * 3}s`} repeatCount="indefinite" path="M-10 116 L150 116" />
                      <animate attributeName="opacity" dur="6s" begin={`-${k * 3}s`} repeatCount="indefinite" values="0;1;1;0" keyTimes="0;.1;.85;1" />
                    </use>
                  ))}
                  <text x="12" y="30" class="say">Walk-in customers only</text>
                </g>
              )}
              {c.scene === 'speed' && (
                <g>
                  {[['Mon', 'Brief', 'i-doc'], ['Tue', 'Wait', 'i-clock'], ['Wed', 'Review', 'i-person'], ['Thu', 'Wait', 'i-clock'], ['Fri', 'Live', 'i-check']].map(([d, what, ico], k) => (
                    <g class={`day d${k}`}>
                      <rect x={8 + k * 62} y="34" width="56" height="92" rx="8" class="daybox" />
                      <text x={36 + k * 62} y="54" text-anchor="middle" class="say">{d}</text>
                      <use href={`#${ico}`} x={24 + k * 62} y="64" width="24" height="24" class="dayico" />
                      <text x={36 + k * 62} y="112" text-anchor="middle" class="say sm">{what}</text>
                    </g>
                  ))}
                  <rect x="8" y="140" width="304" height="8" rx="4" class="track" />
                  <rect x="8" y="140" width="304" height="8" rx="4" class="slowbar" />
                  <text x="160" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="say">5 days for one small change</text>
                </g>
              )}
              {c.scene === 'agency' && (
                <g>
                  <path d="M6 146 H314" class="floor" />
                  <use href="#i-bag" x="14" y="70" width="46" height="46" class="brand" />
                  <text x="37" y="136" text-anchor="middle" class="say sm">Your brands</text>
                  <path id="cs-cash" d="M64 92 C 130 60, 190 60, 236 92" class="wire" />
                  {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((k) => (
                    <use href="#i-dollar" width="22" height="22" x="-11" y="-11" class="coin">
                      <animateMotion dur="2.8s" begin={`-${k * 0.7}s`} repeatCount="indefinite"><mpath href="#cs-cash" /></animateMotion>
                    </use>
                  ))}
                  <rect x="236" y="54" width="70" height="92" class="bld" />
                  {[0, 1, 2].map((r) => [0, 1].map((cc) => <rect x={248 + cc * 26} y={66 + r * 24} width="18" height="14" class="win" />))}
                  <text x="271" y="42" text-anchor="middle" class="say">Agencies</text>
                  <text x="12" y="30" class="say">Every month, out the door</text>
                </g>
              )}
            </svg>
            <p class="cs-say">{c.before}</p>
          </figure>

          <div class="cs-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span>→</span></div>

          {/* AFTER */}
          <figure class="cs-panel cs-after">
            <figcaption class="cs-cap"><span class="cs-pill cs-pill-on">After</span><b>{c.afterHead}</b></figcaption>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 320 170" aria-hidden="true" data-anim>
              {c.scene === 'shop' && (
                <g>
                  {/* the same shop, now selling three ways */}
                  <rect x="10" y="70" width="70" height="56" class="bld" />
                  <path d="M4 70 h82 l-6 -14 h-70 z" class="awn" />
                  <rect x="36" y="96" width="18" height="30" class="door" />
                  {[[34, 'Online', 'i-page', 'i-bag'], [88, 'Companies', 'i-box', 'i-box'], [142, 'Better prices', 'i-dollar', 'i-dollar']].map(([y, label, ico, mover], k) => (
                    <g>
                      <path id={`cs-sh${k}`} d={`M84 98 C 140 98, 150 ${Number(y) + 12}, 214 ${Number(y) + 12}`} class="wire" />
                      <use href={`#${mover}`} width="18" height="18" x="-9" y="-9" class="mover">
                        <animateMotion dur="2.4s" begin={`-${k * 0.8}s`} repeatCount="indefinite"><mpath href={`#cs-sh${k}`} /></animateMotion>
                      </use>
                      <use href={`#${ico}`} x="216" y={Number(y) - 2} width="28" height="28" class="dest" />
                      <text x="250" y={Number(y) + 17} class="say sm">{label}</text>
                    </g>
                  ))}
                </g>
              )}
              {c.scene === 'speed' && (
                <g>
                  {/* the phone chat: ask, and it is live */}
                  <rect x="96" y="8" width="128" height="156" rx="18" class="phone" />
                  <rect x="146" y="16" width="28" height="5" rx="2.5" class="notch" />
                  <g class="b1"><rect x="112" y="34" width="100" height="36" rx="10" class="bub-me" /><text x="162" y="50" text-anchor="middle" class="bub-t on">Change the price</text><text x="162" y="63" text-anchor="middle" class="bub-t on">to $29</text></g>
                  <g class="b2"><rect x="108" y="80" width="104" height="36" rx="10" class="bub-it" /><text x="160" y="96" text-anchor="middle" class="bub-t">Done — it's live</text><use href="#i-check" x="148" y="100" width="14" height="14" class="ok" /></g>
                  <g class="b3"><use href="#i-clock" x="116" y="128" width="20" height="20" class="clk" /><text x="142" y="143" class="say">Minutes</text></g>
                </g>
              )}
              {c.scene === 'agency' && (
                <g>
                  <path d="M6 146 H314" class="floor" />
                  {/* money stays in the jar; the system makes the content */}
                  <path d="M22 60 h60 v80 a6 6 0 0 1 -6 6 h-48 a6 6 0 0 1 -6 -6 z" class="jar" />
                  <rect x="24" y="62" width="56" height="82" class="jar-fill" />
                  <use href="#i-dollar" x="38" y="86" width="28" height="28" class="coin-in" />
                  <text x="52" y="44" text-anchor="middle" class="say">Kept</text>
                  <rect x="118" y="64" width="60" height="60" rx="12" class="machine" />
                  <g><use href="#i-gear" x="130" y="76" width="36" height="36" class="gearc" /><animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="rotate" from="0 148 94" to="360 148 94" dur="3s" repeatCount="indefinite" /></g>
                  <text x="148" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="say sm">Your system</text>
                  {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((k) => <use href="#i-doc" x={206 + (k % 3) * 34} y={96 - Math.floor(k / 3) * 36} width="30" height="30" class={`page p${k}`} />)}
                  <text x="258" y="44" text-anchor="middle" class="say">5–10× content</text>
                </g>
              )}
            </svg>
            <p class="cs-say">{c.after}</p>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <dl class="cs-metrics">
          {c.metrics.map(([v, l]) => <div><dt>{l}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>

        <details>
          <summary>Read the full story</summary>
          <div class="cs-story">
            {c.story.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
            <h4>{c.listTitle}</h4>
            <ul>{c.list.map((li) => <li>{li}</li>)}</ul>
            {c.links.length > 0 && <p class="cs-links">{c.links.map((l) => <a href={l.href}>{l.label} →</a>)}</p>}
          </div>
        </details>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  document.querySelectorAll<SVGSVGElement>('.cs [data-anim]').forEach((svg) => {
    if (reduce) { svg.pauseAnimations(); svg.classList.add('paused'); return; }
    new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => {
      if (e.isIntersecting) { svg.unpauseAnimations(); svg.classList.remove('paused'); }
      else { svg.pauseAnimations(); svg.classList.add('paused'); }
    }).observe(svg);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .cs { max-width: 80rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 6rem 1.5rem 3rem; scroll-margin-top: 64px; }
  .cs-eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-accent); }
  .cs-head h2 { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 64px); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.03em; margin: 14px 0 12px; }
  .cs-head p { color: var(--soft); font-size: 17px; margin: 0; max-width: 60ch; }
  .cs-list { display: grid; gap: 24px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .cs-card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 16px; padding: 26px 26px 18px; }
  .cs-top { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px 16px; }
  .cs-tag { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-accent); border: 1px solid rgba(240, 96, 0, .4); border-radius: 999px; padding: 5px 10px; }
  .cs-top h3 { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 30px); letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0; }

  .cs-ba { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 20px; align-items: stretch; }
  .cs-panel { margin: 0; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 16px 16px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; min-width: 0; }
  .cs-after { border-color: rgba(240, 96, 0, .45); }
  .cs-cap { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cs-cap b { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.25; color: var(--fg); }
  .cs-pill { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 4px 9px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); color: var(--muted); }
  .cs-pill-on { background: var(--color-accent-fill); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); font-weight: 700; }
  .cs-panel svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .cs-say { margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--soft); }
  .cs-arrow { display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .cs-arrow span { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-accent-fill); color: var(--on-accent); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; }

  .cs-metrics { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 18px 20px; margin: 22px 0 0; }
  .cs-metrics div { display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 10px; }
  .cs-metrics dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 36px); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--fg); }
  .cs-metrics div:first-child dd { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .cs-metrics dt { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.35; margin-top: 4px; }
  .cs-card details { margin-top: 18px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-border); padding-top: 10px; }
  .cs-card summary { cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-text-secondary); list-style: none; padding: 6px 0; }
  .cs-card summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .cs-card summary::before { content: "+ "; color: var(--color-accent); }
  .cs-card details[open] summary::before { content: "− "; }
  .cs-card summary:focus-visible, .cs-links a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--fg); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .cs-story { max-width: 70ch; padding-top: 8px; }
  .cs-story p { color: var(--soft); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .cs-story h4 { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 16px 0 6px; }
  .cs-story ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; color: var(--soft); font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.6; display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .cs-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 20px; }
  .cs-links a { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  /* the drawings — one scene per story */
  svg .say { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; fill: var(--fg); }
  svg .say.sm { font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--muted); }
  svg .floor { stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 2; }
  svg .wire { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 2; stroke-dasharray: 4 5; }
  svg .bld { fill: var(--panel-2); stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 2; }
  svg .awn { fill: #f06000; }
  svg .awn-s { fill: var(--panel); opacity: .9; }
  svg .door { fill: var(--line-strong); }
  svg .win { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--water-ink) 25%, var(--panel)); stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  svg .walker { color: var(--muted); }
  svg .mover { color: #f06000; }
  svg .dest { color: var(--fg); }
  svg .dest, svg .mover { animation: cs-pop 2.4s ease-in-out infinite; transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center; }
  @keyframes cs-pop { 0%, 70%, 100% { transform: scale(1); } 85% { transform: scale(1.15); } }
  /* speed: the week crawls */
  svg .daybox { fill: var(--panel-2); stroke: var(--line-strong); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  svg .dayico { color: var(--muted); }
  svg .day { animation: cs-day 8s infinite; }
  svg .d1 { animation-delay: 1.6s; } svg .d2 { animation-delay: 3.2s; } svg .d3 { animation-delay: 4.8s; } svg .d4 { animation-delay: 6.4s; }
  @keyframes cs-day { 0%, 20%, 100% { opacity: .45; } 2%, 18% { opacity: 1; } }
  svg .track { fill: var(--grid-major); }
  svg .slowbar { fill: #f06000; transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: left; animation: cs-bar 8s linear infinite; }
  @keyframes cs-bar { from { transform: scaleX(0); } to { transform: scaleX(1); } }
  svg .phone { fill: var(--panel-2); stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 2.5; }
  svg .notch { fill: var(--fg); }
  svg .bub-me { fill: #f06000; }
  svg .bub-it { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--line-strong); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  svg .bub-t { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--fg); }
  svg .bub-t.on { fill: #000; }
  svg .ok { color: #1f9d55; }
  svg .clk { color: #f06000; }
  svg .b1, svg .b2, svg .b3 { animation: cs-chat 5s infinite; }
  svg .b2 { animation-name: cs-chat2; } svg .b3 { animation-name: cs-chat3; }
  @keyframes cs-chat { 0%, 4% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); } 10%, 92% { opacity: 1; transform: none; } 100% { opacity: 0; } }
  @keyframes cs-chat2 { 0%, 30% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); } 38%, 92% { opacity: 1; transform: none; } 100% { opacity: 0; } }
  @keyframes cs-chat3 { 0%, 50% { opacity: 0; } 58%, 92% { opacity: 1; } 100% { opacity: 0; } }
  /* agency: coins leave vs coins stay */
  svg .brand { color: var(--fg); }
  svg .coin { color: #f06000; }
  svg .jar { fill: none; stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 2.5; }
  svg .jar-fill { fill: color-mix(in srgb, #f06000 30%, var(--panel)); transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: bottom; animation: cs-fill 5s ease-in-out infinite; }
  @keyframes cs-fill { 0% { transform: scaleY(.15); } 80%, 100% { transform: scaleY(1); } }
  svg .coin-in { color: #f06000; }
  svg .machine { fill: var(--panel-accent); stroke: #f06000; stroke-width: 2; }
  svg .gearc { color: #f06000; }
